@title Ridge Racer - boot to the title screen and press PLAY
@game  PCSE00001
@shot-every 100

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Boots the title through its logo sequence to the RIDGE RACER title screen and
# presses PLAY, which is the entry to the front-end menus.
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED (lessons for the next agent)
# - Judge this title ONLY through `vitaslop-desktop --headless`. Its draws are
#   fragment-shader passes, and the software rasterizer `play` uses cannot show
#   them - its shots come out blank and prove nothing. Use
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY to see the sequence rather than one last frame.
# - Boot landmarks on the display-flip clock, measured: legal notice to ~f350,
#   BANDAI NAMCO Games ~f400-550, namco ~f600-750, CELLIUS ~f800-1050, a
#   save-data spinner ~f1050, then the title movie is attempted and skipped
#   (there is no H.264 decoder) and the RIDGE RACER title screen with its
#   pulsing PLAY button is up from ~f1400 and stays up waiting for input.
# - The movie matters: the title IGNORES a failed sceMp4OpenFile and calls
#   sceMp4StartFileStreaming anyway, so the skip needs BOTH to fail honestly.
#   Behind the title screen there should be a movie playing; this run has a
#   plain dark background there instead, and the engine says so on stderr.
# ============================================================================

# --- press PLAY on the title screen ---
# The button's centre is MEASURED off a title-screen shot at screen (480, 420);
# the front touch panel is screen*2, so that is panel (960, 840). The first
# attempt tapped panel y=560..640 - screen y=280..320 - which is empty space
# above the button, and nothing happened for 1100 frames. Measure the button in
# a shot before assuming where a front-end control is.
0: @section boot

1500: touch=960,840
1520:
1560: touch=960,840
1580:
